# Pull request before merge

`main` is protected by process: **create a pull request before any merge**.

## Required

- Do all work on a feature branch. Do not commit to `main`.
- After the first meaningful commit, **push the branch and open a pull request**.
- Keep that PR updated as you iterate (push, then update the PR description if the work changed).
- Do not merge (and do not enable auto-merge) unless the user explicitly asks to merge.

## Forbidden

- Pushing commits directly to `main`
- Fast-forwarding or resetting `main` to land work without a PR
- Merging from the CLI (`git merge`, `git rebase` onto `main` + push, `gh pr merge`) when no PR exists
- Treating “the branch is pushed” as done — the PR is the merge gate

## Cloud / Cursor agents

Use the pull-request tool (`ManagePullRequest`) to open or update the PR. Do not use `gh pr create` / `gh pr merge` for that. PRs default to draft unless the user asks otherwise.
